 ### Durable product decisions
 
+- The root floor game now imports this campaign module as its shared five-day rules and save schema. Keep sale amounts, ownership splits, refunds, patience and migration consistent between both views. Different web origins still have separate browser save slots.
+- Real floor time consumes one patience/action unit per 20 seconds at 1x, with 2x/4x multipliers; consultation reading is paused and committed actions consume time. Hide/background pauses the floor. Do not animate a business clock without applying the same wait cost.
+- Rival decisions belong below the face. Use MobileScroll for the consultation's scrolling controls, with the portrait/header outside it. Reveal products after the first question. Show order totals and the player's credited share before closing; yielding to Lu Yao credits half, and refunds reverse only that share.
+
 - The player is the new beauty advisor Xu Yuan, embodied by the counter-facing camera, work badge, hands/tools, and the consequences of direct service actions. Do not represent the player as an autonomous map sprite.
 - The ordinary business view is a compact, fixed cosmetics-counter stage. NPC movement and ambient activity make the shop feel alive, but player locomotion is not a game mechanic.
 - Entering a customer consultation is immediate. Location changes such as fetching stock are time-costing state transitions, not walking animations.
